1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,000
这周，美国得州。一辆特斯拉跑车，头朝下，开过了一条倒挂的轨道。
This week in Texas, a Tesla sports car drove upside down along an inverted track.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,830
翻个身，落地，再从五辆车的头顶上，一跳而过。
It flipped, landed, and then jumped clean over five cars.

3
00:00:09,830 --> 00:00:17,460
先算个小账：五辆车排起来大约二十五米。斜着起跳，每秒十六米就够，相当于时速五十多公里。
Quick math: five cars in a row are about 25 meters. Launch at an angle and 16 m/s is enough, about 56 km/h.

4
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:22,550
在空中只待两秒多。这一跳难的不是距离，是落地别把车摔坏。
That's just over two seconds in the air. The hard part isn't the distance. It's landing without wrecking the car.

5
00:00:22,550 --> 00:00:26,650
马斯克说：这就是将来量产的那辆车，二零二八年。
Musk says this is the actual production car, coming in 2028.

6
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:32,650
其实这辆车二零一七年就发布过，当时承诺：一点九秒破百，续航一千公里。
This car was first unveiled in 2017, promising 0 to 60 in 1.9 seconds and 1,000 km of range.

7
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:39,830
二零一八年马斯克又说，要给它加个 SpaceX 套件：车身一圈小喷口。今天，喷口真的来了。
In 2018 Musk promised a SpaceX package: small thrusters around the body. Today, the thrusters showed up.

8
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:46,310
三个黑科技：吸在天花板上、一秒破百、会飞。今天不站队，我们一个一个算账。
Three tricks: sticking to the ceiling, 0 to 60 in a second, and flying. No sides today. We do the math.

9
00:00:46,310 --> 00:00:49,720
今天的主角：小 R，一辆有点紧张的跑车。
Today's star: R, a slightly nervous sports car.

10
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:54,040
黑科技一：倒着开，车重两吨，为什么掉不下来？
Trick one: upside down, two tons of car. Why doesn't it fall?

11
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:59,130
车底藏着几台风扇，拼命把车底的空气往外抽，车底气压变低。
Fans hidden underneath pump air out from under the car, so the pressure there drops.

12
00:00:59,130 --> 00:01:03,400
而头顶上，是整个大气层：每平方米，压着十吨。
Above it sits the whole atmosphere: ten tons on every square meter.

13
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:09,050
车底大约八平方米，只要比外面低百分之五，就多出四吨的力，把车按住。
The floor is about eight square meters. Just five percent lower pressure gives four tons pressing the car on.

14
00:01:09,050 --> 00:01:12,660
四吨按着两吨的车：倒过来，也掉不下去。
Four tons holding a two-ton car: even upside down, it stays put.

15
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:18,830
反过来说：风扇一停，四吨变零。倒挂开车的时候，风扇比轮子还要命。
Flip side: if the fans stop, four tons becomes zero. Upside down, the fans matter more than the wheels.

16
00:01:18,830 --> 00:01:23,470
特斯拉屏幕上写的更猛：四千七百公斤，车重的两倍多。
Tesla's screen claimed even more: 4,700 kg, over twice the car's weight.

17
00:01:23,470 --> 00:01:28,700
科技媒体说，这个数可能有水分。不过我们算的四吨，已经够用。
Tech press suspect that's inflated. But our four tons is already enough.

18
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:34,750
这招一点不新：一九七八年，F1 赛车 BT46B，屁股上装了个大风扇。
And it isn't new: in 1978 the F1 car BT46B had a giant fan on its back.

19
00:01:34,750 --> 00:01:40,490
只比了一场，赢了。然后就被叫停：对手说它是吸尘器，还往后喷石子。
It raced once and won. Then it was pulled: rivals called it a vacuum cleaner that sprayed stones.

20
00:01:40,490 --> 00:01:44,620
后来，F1 干脆禁了风扇车，一禁就是四十多年。
F1 later banned fan cars outright, and the ban has lasted over forty years.

21
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:49,580
风扇最狠的地方：机翼要靠速度才有下压力，风扇停着就有。
Here's the killer feature: wings need speed for downforce. Fans work standing still.

22
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:54,120
机翼的下压力跟速度的平方走：速度减半，只剩四分之一。
Wing downforce goes with speed squared: half the speed, a quarter of the force.

23
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:59,710
所以风扇车在弯道最占便宜：车速一慢，机翼没劲了，风扇照样吸。
So fan cars shine in corners: when speed drops, wings go weak, but fans keep sucking.

24
00:01:59,710 --> 00:02:01,910
黑科技一，打分：真本事。
Trick one gets a score: the real thing.

25
00:02:01,910 --> 00:02:06,010
黑科技二：零到六十英里，也就是九十六公里，一秒。
Trick two: 0 to 60 miles an hour, that's 96 km/h, in one second.

26
00:02:06,010 --> 00:02:10,030
一秒钟加到每秒二十七米：加速度，二点七个 g。
Reaching 27 meters per second in one second: that's 2.7 g.

27
00:02:10,030 --> 00:02:13,900
这一秒，只跑了十三米多，差不多三辆车那么长。
In that one second it covers just over 13 meters, about three car lengths.

28
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:20,980
对比一下：现在最快的量产电车，零到六十英里大约一点七秒；F1 赛车两秒半左右。
For comparison: the fastest production EV does 0 to 60 in about 1.7 seconds; an F1 car in about 2.5.

29
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:25,950
可车是靠轮胎抓地往前推的。最好的轮胎，也就一点几个 g。
But a car pushes through its tires, and the best tires manage only 1-point-something g.

30
00:02:25,950 --> 00:02:30,350
第一招：风扇把车压紧。压得越紧，轮胎抓得越牢。
Fix one: the fans press the car down. The harder the press, the better the grip.

31
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:35,290
第二招更狠：干脆不靠地面，车尾向后喷气，就像火箭。
Fix two, more brutal: forget the road. Blast gas out the back, like a rocket.

32
00:02:35,290 --> 00:02:38,840
据报道，后面四个喷口，推力约八万牛。
Reportedly, the four rear jets make about 80,000 newtons.

33
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:43,730
八万牛除以两吨，每秒提速四十米：四个 g。光靠喷气就够了。
80,000 newtons over two tons is 40 meters per second squared: 4 g. The jets alone are enough.

34
00:02:43,730 --> 00:02:48,090
但喷气只够喷一两秒，所以它是专门给起步那一下准备的。
But the jets only last a second or two, so they're made for that one launch.

35
00:02:48,090 --> 00:02:51,900
不过，还没有独立测量。这个“一秒”，先打个问号。
No independent test yet, though. That 'one second' gets a question mark.

36
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:59,310
黑科技三，重头戏：它到底能飞多久？官方只给了两个数：十个喷口，六百升压缩空气。
Trick three, the main event: how long can it fly? Tesla gave two numbers: ten jets, 600 liters of compressed air.

37
00:02:59,310 --> 00:03:07,440
六百升，就是三个浴缸。压到三百个大气压，大约装两百公斤空气；压到七百，也就三百多公斤。
600 liters is three bathtubs. At 300 atmospheres that's about 200 kg of air; at 700, just over 300.

38
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:14,030
冷空气喷出去，每秒最多六七百米。推力八万牛，除一下：每秒要喷掉一百三十公斤。
Cold air leaves at 600 to 700 meters per second at most. 80 kN divided by that: 130 kg every second.

39
00:03:14,030 --> 00:03:19,700
两百公斤，每秒一百三，一秒半见底。而且压力一掉，推力跟着掉。
200 kg at 130 per second: empty in a second and a half. And as pressure drops, so does thrust.

40
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:25,840
只悬停呢？两吨的车要两万牛，每秒三十多公斤：五到十秒，就得落地。
Just hovering? Two tons needs 20 kN, over 30 kg a second: down again in five to ten seconds.

41
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:33,260
那为什么不喷火？火箭燃料喷速每秒三千米，是冷空气的五倍：同样的推力，只要五分之一的料。
Why not use fire? Rocket exhaust leaves at 3,000 m/s, five times faster than cold air: same thrust, a fifth of the propellant.

42
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:39,320
可车上烧火箭燃料，路边的人就不是被石子砸，是被烤了。所以只能喷冷气。
But burn rocket fuel on a car, and bystanders don't get pelted with gravel. They get roasted. So: cold air.

43
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:44,410
冷气推进其实很常见：卫星在太空里调姿态，喷的就是冷气。
Cold-gas thrusters are actually common: satellites use them to adjust their attitude in space.

44
00:03:44,410 --> 00:03:47,980
不信？我们做了一个虚拟实验，你可以自己调。
Don't believe us? We built a virtual lab. Try it yourself.

45
00:03:47,980 --> 00:03:51,350
三百个大气压，悬停三米：五秒左右。
300 atmospheres, hover at three meters: about five seconds.

46
00:03:51,350 --> 00:03:54,090
压到七百个大气压：十秒左右。
Squeeze it to 700: about ten seconds.

47
00:03:54,090 --> 00:03:57,180
再把车减掉五百公斤：也就十二秒多。
Then cut 500 kg off the car: just over twelve.

48
00:03:57,180 --> 00:04:02,930
注意：车减掉四分之一，时间只多了两秒多。瓶颈是罐子，不是车重。
Notice: cut a quarter of the weight and you gain only two seconds. The bottleneck is the tank, not the car.

49
00:04:02,930 --> 00:04:09,810
还有隐藏减益：气体一膨胀就降温，罐子越喷越冷，压力掉得更快，喷口还会结霜。
Hidden penalty: expanding gas cools, the tank gets colder, pressure falls faster, and nozzles frost.

50
00:04:09,810 --> 00:04:14,730
结论：这不是飞，是用两百公斤空气，换来的一次很贵的跳。
Verdict: it doesn't fly. It trades 200 kg of air for one very expensive jump.

51
00:04:14,730 --> 00:04:19,410
不过，跳得有派头，也是真功夫：它在空中怎么翻跟头？
Still, a stylish jump takes skill. How does it flip in mid-air?

52
00:04:19,410 --> 00:04:25,390
秘密是：喷口不对准重心。推力偏一点，就变成让车转动的力，叫力矩。
The secret: the jets don't point through the center of mass. Off-center thrust turns the car. That's torque.

53
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:31,350
力矩等于推力乘距离：假如偏一米，八万牛就是八万牛米，翻一辆车绰绰有余。
Torque is thrust times distance: off by one meter, 80,000 newtons makes 80,000 newton-meters. Plenty to flip a car.

54
00:04:31,350 --> 00:04:37,430
前面喷、后面不喷，车头抬起来；左边喷、右边不喷，车就打滚。
Fire the front but not the back, and the nose lifts. Fire the left but not the right, and it rolls.

55
00:04:37,430 --> 00:04:43,460
十个喷口一起配合，就能在空中“开”车。火箭回收落地，用的也是这一招。
Ten jets together let it steer in the air. Rockets that land themselves use the same trick.

56
00:04:43,460 --> 00:04:50,010
再烧一点脑：同样托起两吨，直升机能在天上待一个小时，喷口为什么只能撑几秒？
A brain-burner: a helicopter holds up two tons for an hour. Why do jets last only seconds?

57
00:04:50,010 --> 00:04:56,420
推力，是每秒喷出的空气乘速度；花的力气，却是空气乘速度的平方，再除以二。
Thrust is air per second times speed. But the energy you spend is air times speed squared, over two.

58
00:04:56,420 --> 00:05:02,930
速度翻一倍，推力翻一倍，力气翻四倍。所以想省力：多推空气，推得慢一点。
Double the speed: double the thrust, four times the energy. So to save energy, push more air, more slowly.

59
00:05:02,930 --> 00:05:08,000
喷口：每秒三十公斤空气，六百多米每秒，功率六千多千瓦。
Jets: 30 kg of air a second at over 600 m/s. That's over 6,000 kilowatts.

60
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:13,040
十米的旋翼：每秒推一吨空气，只要二十米每秒，约两百千瓦。
A ten-meter rotor: a ton of air a second at just 20 m/s. About 200 kilowatts.

61
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:18,550
差了三十倍。所以真正在做飞行汽车的公司，造出来的都长着螺旋桨。
Thirty times apart. That's why companies building real flying cars all use propellers.

62
00:05:18,550 --> 00:05:23,350
无人机为什么都是大桨慢转？同一个道理：桨越大，越省电。
Why do drones use big, slow propellers? Same reason: the bigger the blade, the less power.

63
00:05:23,350 --> 00:05:28,200
黑科技三，打分：物理没错，但它是表演，不是交通工具。
Trick three gets a score: right physics, but a stunt, not transportation.

64
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:33,800
好，假设你就坐在里面。起步四个 g，跟过山车最猛的那一下差不多。
Now imagine you're inside. Launching at 4 g is like the wildest moment on a roller coaster.

65
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:38,870
四个 g 的时候，你七十公斤的身体，压在座椅上有两百八十公斤。
At 4 g, your 70 kg body presses into the seat like 280 kg.

66
00:05:38,870 --> 00:05:45,820
翻跟头时头朝下，血往脑袋里冲。科技媒体都在问：要不要穿战斗机飞行员的抗荷服？
Upside down, blood rushes to your head. Tech press ask: will you need a fighter pilot's g-suit?

67
00:05:45,820 --> 00:05:51,430
车里每个空隙，都塞满了碳纤维缠绕的高压气罐，压力是轮胎的上百倍。
Every gap inside is packed with carbon-fiber-wrapped tanks, at over a hundred times tire pressure.

68
00:05:51,430 --> 00:05:56,880
这种罐子又轻又结实，但 SpaceX 几次火箭出事，都和这类罐子有关。
They're light and strong, but this type of tank has been linked to SpaceX rocket failures.

69
00:05:56,880 --> 00:06:02,340
还有路边的人：据报道，演示时喷气卷起的碎石沙子，能飞出几十米。
And bystanders: reportedly the blast threw gravel and sand tens of meters during the demo.

70
00:06:02,340 --> 00:06:08,320
再算一笔账：把气罐充满，最理想也要二十多度电，够这辆车跑一百多公里。
One more sum: filling the tanks takes, ideally, over 20 kWh. That would drive this car over 100 km.

71
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:14,000
按家里的电价，一跳也就十几块钱。真正贵的，是那些罐子和风险。
At household electricity prices, one jump costs a couple of dollars. The expensive part is the tanks and the risk.

72
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:19,350
马斯克自己说：安全不是主要目标；他们会“争取不害死任何人”。
Musk himself said safety is not the main goal, and they will 'aspire not to kill anyone'.

73
00:06:19,350 --> 00:06:21,710
这是原话，我们不加评论。
Those are his words. No comment from us.

74
00:06:21,710 --> 00:06:22,980
好，打分表。
OK, the scorecard.

75
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:27,160
吸地：真本事，一九七八年就有，现在做得更猛。
Suction: real, around since 1978, now turned up.

76
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:30,590
一秒破百：物理上说得通，等独立测量。
One-second sprint: physically plausible, awaiting independent tests.

77
00:06:30,590 --> 00:06:34,580
飞：几秒钟的表演。很酷，但别指望它带你上班。
Flying: a few seconds of show. Cool, but it won't fly you to work.

78
00:06:34,580 --> 00:06:40,360
时间表：二零一七年就发布过，推迟了一次又一次，现在说二零二八年量产。
Timeline: first unveiled in 2017, delayed again and again, now promised for 2028.

79
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:45,780
对一下账：一点九秒变成了一秒，交车从二零二零年变成了二零二八年。
Check the books: 1.9 seconds became 1, and delivery went from 2020 to 2028.

80
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:50,390
最后一个彩蛋：马斯克说，也许会开着它飞越蛇河峡谷。
One last easter egg: Musk said it might jump the Snake River Canyon.

81
00:06:50,390 --> 00:06:57,240
一九七四年，有个特技演员骑着火箭摩托试过：降落伞提前打开，他飘进了峡谷底。
In 1974 a stuntman tried it on a rocket bike. His parachute opened early and he drifted into the canyon.

82
00:06:57,240 --> 00:07:00,670
要是小 R 真飞过去了，我们再做一期。
If R actually makes it, we'll make another episode.

83
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:04,320
下期见。小 R，别紧张，你今天表现不错。
See you next time. Relax, R. You did great today.

84
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:15,630
友情提示：吸力、一秒破百、六百升是特斯拉的说法；八万牛来自媒体报道；空气量、飞行时间、功率和电量，是我们按常见数值做的估算。
Note: the suction, the one-second sprint and 600 liters are Tesla's claims; 80 kN is from press reports; air mass, airtime, power and energy are our estimates.

